<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Cleartext HTTP exists in this app for exactly one reason: the amplifier relay
  (Shelly 1 Gen4). The Shelly Gen2+ JSON-RPC API is plain HTTP on the centre's
  own WiFi, and modern Android blocks cleartext by default, so without this the
  Test button and every switch would fail.

  Centre-local WiFi only. The app never exposes the relay API publicly, never
  talks to Shelly Cloud, and has no other network use of any kind.

  Why this is not narrowed to RFC 1918 ranges: Android's network security
  config matches *hostnames*, not IP ranges — <domain> does not accept CIDR
  (10.0.0.0/8 and friends are rejected as invalid hostnames), and the relay
  address is typed by staff at setup time, so it cannot be enumerated here.
  The narrowing is therefore in code instead: relay/ShellyClient.kt is the only
  networking in the app, it only ever builds http://<relay_host>/rpc/... from
  the `relay_host` setting, and nothing else opens a connection.

  If the relay is ever given a fixed address by policy, replace the base-config
  below with a <domain-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true"> listing that
  literal host, and set the base config back to false.
-->
<network-security-config>
    <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true">
        <trust-anchors>
            <certificates src="system" />
        </trust-anchors>
    </base-config>
</network-security-config>
